    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"417769\">Bulhwi Cha</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/116395-maths/topic/accessibility.20and.20descending.20chains/near/581319468\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I also wonder whether there are any textbooks that cover the accessibility predicate in detail.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Saying that a is accessible in a preorder is the same thing as saying <code>Iio a</code> is well-founded.</p>",
        "id": 581610332,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1774443754
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That's right! I also wanted to know as many interesting facts as possible, even when the binary relation is not a preorder. Here's my Lean code about the accessibility predicate: <a href=\"https://git.sr.ht/~chabulhwi/tpil-solutions/tree/master/item/TPIL/Chapter08/Accessibility.lean\">https://git.sr.ht/~chabulhwi/tpil-solutions/tree/master/item/TPIL/Chapter08/Accessibility.lean</a>.</p>",
        "id": 581622556,
